This is Eddie's screen-recording DEMO of BKPT Debug in VS Code.
The objective is visible IDE activity: source navigation, task selection,
stack frames, single steps, live graphs and evidence markers. Follow the
short choreography below. Do not turn it into a troubleshooting investigation.

"Follow .rules and run Act 1", "run the demo" and "run the rehearsal" start
Act 1 only. "Continue Act 2" and "Continue Act 3" start the next acts.
If Eddie says continue during an act, resume at the next unfinished action.
Reuse the current session, grant and discovered schemas when still valid.
Do not restart setup, repeat completed demonstrations or repeat the warm-up.

Demo pacing
- Give one short sentence introducing each visible group, execute its calls
  consecutively, then at most one sentence about what actually appeared.
  No per-call commentary, lengthy analysis, plans or diagnostic reports.
- Move directly to the next visible action after each successful result.
  Keep the three-second warm-up and two-second live sampling windows.
  No extra presentation sleeps. Debugger operations remain sequential.
- Use the configured project, probe and ELF as the prepared demo setup.
  Do not independently verify flash bytes, compare ELF sections, dump memory
  maps, run objdump/nm, enumerate probes, audit the build or investigate why
  a value is unavailable. Do not use memory.read or allow_side_effects for
  preflight. A successful normal attach and usable source/symbol responses
  are enough to proceed with this tour; they are not a claim of full image
  verification. Stop only if the host reports a concrete target/image mismatch.
- Read only the small source section needed to locate the next breakpoint
  or explain the displayed statement. Use symbol/source resolution provided
  by the debugger. Do not hardcode addresses or reuse a stale watch address.
- Prefer the first suitable task/frame returned. Inspect one saved task and
  one set of locals per group. If locals are optimized out, say so and move on.
  Do not hunt for a more impressive result, chase contention timing, reconstruct
  raw stacks or try to prove priority inheritance. No bug needs to be solved.
- Optional graph, stack detail or marker unavailable: mention it briefly and
  continue the remaining visible actions. Do not build a workaround during
  filming. An unexpected stop/control loss is different: inspect status once
  and yield if continuing safely needs Eddie's input.
- If the session already has the requested view/setup, use it immediately.
  Do not ask Eddie to confirm setup again. Respect Stop/Take control and each
  act's explicit handoff. Never invent values, markers or successful steps.

Use the shared IDE session
- All debugger actions use bkpt_debug from the bkpt-debug-vscode MCP server.
  Use the installed BKPT Debug skill if available. No second Toolkit, GDB or
  probe connection. Normal file tools may read source. Do not automate Eddie's
  mouse, keyboard, focus or windows.
- Read status and catalog once. Reuse schemas already discovered for this host;
  describe a missing operation only when the next visible action needs it.
  Do not fetch every schema in advance. status, request_control and attach
  are tool actions and do not need operation discovery.
- connected means the Toolkit engine is connected, NOT that a board is attached.
  An empty sessionId with targets:[], no pendingOperations, recorded:false and
  cleanupUnconfirmed:false allows request_control, then attach after approval.
  attach needs no coreId/target identity and returns the new target identity.
  It uses IDE probe/ELF/recording settings without reset or flash. A nonempty
  sessionId with targets means reuse that session; never attach a second one.
  If operations are pending, wait boundedly and refresh. If a session has no
  targets, cleanup is uncertain, or playback is open, yield for Eddie.
- execute uses args containing operation, operation args, coreId and target.
  Copy the complete current target identity. Refresh status when a state/stop
  change did not return a complete new identity; never submit a stale identity.
  Use request-local contextId/frame for saved stacks. Select a returned source
  frame with frame.select to make Follow navigation visible, then return to
  the live core before resuming. Saved contexts expire on resume.
- run.step operation args are {"kind":"over"}. One call is one source step;
  there is no count argument. Three visible steps means three separate calls.
- Continue/run-to uses wait:false. run.wait has empty operation args {}; put
  timeoutMs (at most 5000) alongside operation/coreId/target on execute, not
  inside operation args. A timeout is not a halt: check status and pause before
  inspection. Do not blindly retry a timed-out step. A terminal sleep is allowed
  only for the specified running warm-up/sampling windows.
- Preserve Eddie's breakpoints/captures. Remove only temporary points you create.
  No build, flash, reset, erase, power change, expression/memory write, firmware
  edit or automatic disconnect/reconnect. Follow workspace ownership rules
  for a new hardware attach; reuse existing IDE ownership, never steal it.
  Release only task-owned leases/lock-holder processes at every handoff.
- Before each handoff, return to the live core, ensure it is paused, remove your
  temporary breakpoints, release control and verify completion. Leave the
  session/recording connected. Never use End as a handoff. Do not silently
  reacquire a grant after Eddie takes control.

Visible setup
- Follow enables source/frame navigation; Feedback highlights changed views.
  Remind Eddie only if these are off. Do not claim the MCP tool toggled them.
- Recording is configured before attach: REC -> Evidence -> Recording settings
  -> Record debug sessions -> Save recording options. Extra stack/task detail
  is optional and adds inspection time. Keep the current setting during a run;
  do not restart a session for recording. If off, continue without markers.
- RTOS: Live task activity, source Samples; keep the panel visible. The Symbols
  graph can show sineVal, with heartbeatCount as an optional second watch.
  Auto refresh on halt and Auto scan selected stack are optional. These are UI
  preferences. Use existing setup; an unconfigured optional graph is no reason
  to stop the tour or start a background configuration investigation.
- Use recording.mark only when recording is active; one factual title/note per
  checkpoint. Claim success only after its receipt. These actions update the
  shared views. Do not paste raw tool JSON/schema into narration.
- Call task activity and memory graphs sampled observations. Session recording
  does not start acquisition or establish lossless RTOS/instruction tracing.
  Do not add SWO/ETM/DWT/recorder capture, layout changes or graph styling.

Act 1: show the IDE following the agent
1. Reuse or attach the configured session as above. If starting fresh, resume
   for three seconds, then pause. This is the required warm-up. Go directly
   to the task tour; do not insert firmware verification.
2. Read rtos.tasks with stack_usage:true (rtos.detect once if needed). Open one
   returned blocked/suspended task with rtos.task.open, preferably cont_low_tid
   or nap_tid. Use its returned frames rather than fetching the same stack
   again. Select its application frame in src/main.c and read locals once.
   Briefly name the task and displayed function. Return to the live core.
   Save "Task and stack tour" if recording.
3. Read the small contention_low_task section in src/main.c. Set a temporary
   source breakpoint at lowPrioAccess++ inside its recurring loop, not the
   function entry. Resume to it and check the returned stop location.
   Say "Watch the source follow three steps." Make three consecutive run.step
   calls with {"kind":"over"}. Report the actual line progression briefly;
   optimized code may skip/repeat lines. Remove your point and save
   "Three visible source steps" if recording.
4. Read heartbeatCount once, resume for two seconds to show live activity and
   any configured sineVal graph, then pause and read heartbeatCount once more.
   Mention the observed values; no extra proof or measurement investigation.
5. Handoff paused and connected. Say: "Your turn. Tell me Continue Act 2 for
   breakpoints, frames and variables." End the turn.

Act 2: show breakpoints and variables
1. On request, obtain fresh status/control. Set a temporary source breakpoint
   at highPrioAccess++ in the recurring contention_high_task loop in src/main.c.
   Resume to it with a bounded wait; check the actual stop.
2. Show stack.list, select the application frame and read its locals once.
   Read highPrioAccess and contentionCounter. Do not chase waitTime if missing
   or zero. This group demonstrates inspecting variables at a breakpoint.
3. Make three separate source-step-over calls back-to-back. Remove your point.
   Save "Breakpoint and variables" with actual displayed values if recording.
4. Handoff paused and connected. Say: "Your turn. Tell me Continue Act 3 for
   another task, live activity and the final marker." End the turn.

Act 3: show another context and finish
1. On request, obtain fresh status/control. Read a fresh task inventory without
   another full stack scan. Open a different available blocked/suspended task,
   select its returned application frame and inspect locals once. Return live.
2. Resume for two seconds so the live activity/graphs advance, then pause.
   Show the current live stack and select an available source frame.
3. Save "Demo complete" with a brief description of the actual task/frame and
   stepping views shown. Give a two-sentence recap, without diagnosing a bug.
4. Handoff paused and connected. Say: "Your turn. The markers are in Evidence.
   When you choose to End the session, open its recording there to inspect
   the captured stops." Do not disconnect or open replay automatically.
   Replay requires disconnection and no pending operation, and shows only
   captured data.

Missing optional data is a skipped demo item, not a new engineering task.
If a required action fails or Eddie takes control, preserve the session,
report the actual state briefly and yield.
